From e85ab020c5bc34320e18050c69db9b6a50fddcac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:43:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Scenario 5: results replayed on EC2 (Ubuntu 24.04, 4 vCPU, 15
 GB)

Same results as the first run in a Linux sandbox. Hydra ETL 0.22.0: reader sees a
mixed pair 1.4 to 1.6 s per run; kill just after the rename overwrites silently,
kill during step 2 is refused until 'hdrctl workflow undo'. With the write-ahead
journal patch both cases are refused and undone. Airflow: mixed state after kill,
next run overwrites silently. Both generation variants: reader never sees a mix,
manifest stays on the previous generation after every kill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011X5H6WN7YFXx8LCdr73MxR
